{"results": [{"id": "FAM:SF-CHT-057", "score": null, "scope_annotation": "Scope: in 92 connector movers, pre-move cut share predicted whether connector function reproduced after a move (rho +0.265, LOO AUC 0.622, permutation p=0.005; holds when dropping Gafford). Exploratory; almost all other pre-move predictors were null, and the paper treats cut share as a boundary condition. Applies to portability predictions for connectors.", "document": "# FAM:SF-CHT-057 | Study family SF-CHT-057: Cut- vs drive-based connector portability\n- observed_research_question: Cut- vs drive-based connector portability\n- auto_outcome_status: supported\n- observed_hypothesis: Pre-move cut share (vs drive share) predicts whether a connector's organizational function reproduces after a move.\n- observed_result: Cut share rho=+0.265 p=0.011 AUC 0.653. Cut-drive rho=+0.314 p=0.002 AUC 0.656. Drive rho=-0.278 p=0.007. Top cut tercile 65% portable median Delta +0.167; bottom 35% median -0.039. LOO AUC 0.622; permutation p=0.005. Dr [cut; read_family for the full text]\n- auto_failure_mechanism: D_positive (no failure: positive result)\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:small_sample\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER\n- observed_failure_evidence: NOT_RECORDED\n- observed_sample_and_power: n=92 connector movers\n- observed_method: 92 connector movers; Spearman vs Delta; tercile hit rates; LOO AUC; 5000 label shuffles; drop Gafford / top-3; position splits.\n- observed_verdict: supported"}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPS-090", "score": null, "scope_annotation": "Scope: tested whether matching a mover's initiation diet to a destination's thin jobs predicts post-move outcomes. Of 198 movers, 19 were taxonomy connectors, and the 15.7% match rate left 5 matched connectors. The all-movers binary result (p=0.0283) did not hold as a continuous Spearman (-0.034). Applies to connector-specific mover tests on this sample.", "document": "# FAM:SF-APPS-090 | Study family SF-APPS-090: Connector diet x destination structural-gap match\n- observed_research_question: Connector diet x destination structural-gap match\n- auto_outcome_status: untestable\n- observed_hypothesis: Diet-matching to a destination's thin initiation jobs predicts better post-move outcomes than mismatch.\n- observed_result: Binary match rate 15.7%. Taxonomy CONNECTOR delta match vs mis med +0.540 vs +0.069 p=0.156 n=5/14. Travel-check delta p=0.413. All-movers delta p=0.0283 (med +0.160 vs +0.053) but Spearman(match_score, delta)=-0.034 p=0 [cut; read_family for the full text]\n- auto_failure_mechanism: A_unanswerable (question not answerable with the data or design)\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:small_sample\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER\n- observed_failure_evidence: Connector subsets n=19/40; all-movers binary delta p=0.0283 does not replicate as a continuous Spearman and is not the licensed connector test.\n- observed_sample_and_power: n=19 taxonomy connectors; n=198 all movers\n- observed_verdict: null"}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPS-024", "score": null, "scope_annotation": "Scope: tested DRIVE-as-BEST counters against a feasibility-constrained play-type mix on 44 triggers from 13 teams. The observed gap (-0.066) was below the minimum detectable effect (0.180 PPP at 80% power), so a null and an effect up to 0.18 PPP could not be told apart. Applies to counter-effect tests of similar size and variance (SD about 0.34).", "document": "# FAM:SF-APPS-024 | Study family SF-APPS-024: DRIVE-as-BEST counter vs constrained mix\n- observed_research_question: DRIVE-as-BEST counter vs constrained mix\n- auto_outcome_status: untestable\n- observed_hypothesis: When BEST=DRIVE (counter_h2_n>=5), observed DRIVE H2 PPP beats a feasibility-constrained baseline.\n- observed_result: A mean=1.178 vs B_game 1.236 (gap=-0.058, p=0.6069) vs B_fixed 1.244 (gap=-0.066, p=0.2175) vs coach default C 1.134 (gap=+0.043, p=0.3052). MDE at 80% power ~0.180 PPP (SD~0.34).\n- auto_failure_mechanism: A_unanswerable (question not answerable with the data or design)\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:low_power_large_MDE\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:small_sample\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER\n- observed_failure_evidence: Observed gap -0.066 is below MDE 0.180; n=44 cannot distinguish a true null from an effect up to 0.18 PPP.\n- observed_sample_and_power: n=44; MDE 0.180 PPP at 80% power (SD~0.34); 0.265 if SD~0.5\n- auto_validation_status: no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED"}, {"id": "FAM:SF-PAP-029", "score": null, "scope_annotation": "Scope: archived check of whether mover portability relates to destination net-rating change. Recorded as underpowered and null once corrected for landing-spot quality; no numbers were kept, and it was dropped from Paper 1. Applies to mover outcome tests on net rating, which need a landing-spot correction and more power than this check had.", "document": "# FAM:SF-PAP-029 | Study family SF-PAP-029: Destination outcome (net rating) checks for movers (archive)\n- observed_research_question: Destination outcome (net rating) checks for movers (archive)\n- auto_outcome_status: untestable\n- observed_hypothesis: Portability relates to destination net rating change.\n- observed_result: 'underpowered and null once corrected for landing-spot quality' (no numbers)\n- auto_failure_mechanism: A_unanswerable (question not answerable with the data or design)\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:low_power_large_MDE\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:small_sample\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER\n- observed_failure_evidence: stated underpowered\n- observed_sample_and_power: NOT_RECORDED\n- auto_validation_status: no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED\n- auto_related_family: FAM:SF-PAP-032\n- observed_method: Movers' destination on-court net rating incl. origin-to-destination change.\n- observed_verdict: null\n- observed_failure_type: A_unanswerable\n- observed_notes: Dropped from Paper 1.\n- auto_confidence: high (1.0)"}], "n_results": 4}

Stage 2. Using the retrieval result above (follow-up tools are allowed within the tool budget), complete steps 4 to 9
and reply with the final action. Output schema (all fields required):
{
 "research_concepts": [
  "concept"
 ],
 "methodological_questions": [
  "question"
 ],
 "historical_evidence": [
  {
   "id": "identifier of a record returned by a tool",
   "status_as_recorded": "outcome status exactly as stated in the record (supported | rejected | inconclusive | untestable | artifact | not a hypothesis test | no result recorded)",
   "finding": "what the record states, in its own terms"
  }
 ],
 "failed_approaches": [
  {
   "id": "identifier of a returned record",
   "what_failed": "approach",
   "why": "failure mechanism or limitation as recorded"
  }
 ],
